import json
from pathlib import Path
from assembly_record_writer import write_record
p=Path(__file__).with_name('assembly_kimel.json')
d=json.loads(p.read_text())
d['kernel']=d['kernel'].replace('Earlier actual OT1999 Records must be screened when this draft is released; no unrelated earlier application changes the presented immunity rule.', 'The effective Flippo, Lesage, Fiore, Drye, Torres and Steamfitters Records were screened: none changes the ADEA text, Article I enforcement rule, state-arm premise or available immunity remedy. Their distinctions between legal capacity and substantive liability do not supply new immunity grounds. Paul and United Reporting have no effective event; Hill remains stopped in the January 11 group and supplies no law or count.')
d['blocks']['Opinion Topology']="| Writing | Author | Joined by | Relationship to judgment | Scope joined |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Opinion of the Court | {AUTHOR} | {FULL_JOINERS} in full; O'Connor and Scalia as to Part I only | Five-Justice reversal and remand | Seven-Justice statutory holding in Part I; five-Justice Article I and reservation/remand in Parts II–III |\n| Dissent from Parts II–III | O'Connor | Scalia, Kennedy, Thomas | Would affirm immunity dismissal | Article I opposition and alternative §5 rejection; O'Connor and Scalia join Part I of the Court's opinion |\n| Separate dissent on statutory authorization | Thomas | Kennedy | Would affirm independently on statutory grounds | Rejects Part I's incorporation reading; also joins O'Connor's constitutional dissent |"
d['blocks']['Separate Writings']="Justice O'Connor, joined by Scalia, Kennedy and Thomas, dissents from the Article I holding and resulting remand. They distinguish a valid federal employment duty from a private action against a nonconsenting State's treasury and expressly seek reconsideration of Florida Prepaid's Article I rule and the Union Gas power conclusion to the necessary extent. They do not claim that a patent-only limitation already governs lower courts or that ordinary age-employment regulation lies outside commerce.\n\nThey also reject §5 as an independent basis for these private remedies. Gregory permits rational age classifications, including imperfect generalizations, whereas the ADEA generally demands more than constitutional rationality. Its bona fide occupational qualification requires reasonable necessity to normal business operation; a reasonable factor other than age does not authorize treatment because of age. Good-cause discipline remains distinct. A protected seniority system must be bona fide and not intended to evade the Act, and cannot permit involuntary age-based retirement of a protected individual. Benefit-plan alternatives require at least equal payment or cost for older workers under the specified regulation, or a voluntary early-retirement incentive consistent with the Act's purposes; neither excuses failure to hire, and benefit plans cannot permit involuntary age-based retirement. The employer bears the stated burden under those seniority and benefit provisions. The foreign-workplace defense requires that compliance violate the foreign country's law and supplies no domestic exception. No defense is found established.\n\nThe four assess the identified governmental complaints, federal-employment newspaper reports, private-sector findings and California survey, principally concerning public-safety age limits, as insufficiently connected to unconstitutional state practices to support this remedy's breadth. They neither infer constitutional validity from state-law permission nor treat unrecovered legislative sources as proof that Congress heard nothing. Boerne requires substantive fit; their objection does not impose formal findings, a number of violations, geographical evidence, a sunset or an individual constitutional-tort prerequisite. Florida Prepaid's preventive property remedy presents, for them, a different protected interest and remedial gap; permitting prevention beyond constitutional violations does not itself settle this statute's fit.\n\nJustice Thomas, joined by Kennedy, additionally dissents from statutory authorization. They distinguish express State-employer coverage from unmistakable authorization of this private federal action. Section 626(c) can be read to supply the ADEA's own cause while §626(b) imports FLSA remedial and procedural incidents. The original 1967 incorporation, the 1974 amendment of §216(b), the later removal of §255's incorporation and the competent-court language leave insufficient clarity in their view. They require no universal single-section formula, but regard this statutory ambiguity as independently sufficient to affirm; their constitutional objections remain alternatives if authorization is assumed."
d['continuity'] += " O'Connor's constitutional dissent is joined by Scalia, Kennedy and Thomas; Thomas's distinct statutory dissent is joined by Kennedy. The public summaries preserve each ground and its limits."
p.write_text(json.dumps(d,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2),encoding='utf-8')
write_record(p,'Ginsburg',d['lead_support'],"Ginsburg is selected for coordinating the combined statutory authorization, independently sufficient Article I ground and explicit reservation of §5 without turning a power ruling into liability or an award. Her Florida Prepaid Article I join and distinct College Savings §5 position demonstrate the component separation this opinion needs. Stevens is the strongest alternative from his Florida Prepaid opinion, and Stone can faithfully apply the same approved ground; Ginsburg offers the concrete fit in keeping these different statutory and power conclusions precise. All three have zero counted leads, while Souter has one; no lower-count alternative defeats the selection. Stone's agreement and office supply no additional self-assignment advantage, and no expansion accommodation is invented.",True)
